@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Rotate a tablet
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Rider" as rider
box "Frontend — Ride app (ride application)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TheClass" as page
  participant "the-class.scss" as sheet
end box
box "Device — Browser" #F2F4F7
  participant "Viewport" as viewport
end box
rider -> viewport : Hold an 11 inch tablet in portrait, 834 x 1194
viewport -> sheet : Evaluate min-width: 64rem
sheet --> viewport : No match: one column that scrolls (L2-171 AC2)
rider -> viewport : Scroll to the end
viewport --> rider : "What the bike will do" ends above the pinned footer; nothing is hidden behind it (L2-171 AC3)
rider -> viewport : Rotate to landscape, 1194 x 834
viewport -> sheet : Evaluate min-width: 64rem again
sheet --> viewport : Match: two columns on one screen, no scrolling (L2-171 AC1)
sheet --> viewport : Footer hidden, the-class~__action shown (L2-171 AC5)
viewport -> page : No component state changes; the same DOM is laid out again
page --> rider : The parked video stays in its box, in the height left at 16:9 (L2-171 AC1)
rider -> viewport : Rotate back to portrait
sheet --> viewport : One column, footer pinned again (L2-171 AC2, AC3)
@enduml
